{"text": "From: Graciela Montenegro <gmontenegro@mal-law.example>\nTo: Conflicts <conflicts@mal-law.example>\nCc: \"Abimbola, Stuart\" <sabimbola@mal-law.example>, Hye-jin Bae <hbae@mal-law.example>\nDate: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 16:42:07 -0700\nSubject: CONFLICT CHECK - new matter - Wetherington / orchard partition - need by Thursday\n\nTeam,\n\nNew Business Intake form is in the system but I want a manual check on this one because of the family overlap. Please run all of the following and reply-all.\n\nPROSPECTIVE CLIENT\nChase Wetherington (goes by his middle name; legal name on the deed is Franklin C. Wetherington)\nDOB 10/30/1978. Driver's license WDL7K29QF41B.\n4410 Naches Heights Road, Yakima, WA 98908\nCell 509-555-0133, chase@wetheringtonorchards.example\n\nADVERSE / RELATED\n1. Jordan Wetherington -- Chase's younger sister, co-owner of the home ranch. Lives in Wenatchee. Jordan is represented by Anton Marchetti (solo, Ellensburg).\n2. Wetherington Family Orchards, Inc. (\"WFO\"), UBI 602 771 348, EIN 91-1740226. Chase and Jordan each hold 50%.\n3. The Wetherington 2009 Irrevocable Trust -- holds the 80 acres on Tieton Drive. Trustee is their mother, Lorraine Zhou (remarried; formerly Lorraine Wetherington -- check both names).\n4. Blue Heron Agricultural Lending, FLCA -- operating line, loan no. 4471-209-88, about $1.9 million outstanding; in default since the August 1 payment. Blue Heron has threatened a receiver.\n5. Cascade Ridge Packing Co. -- packer, claims a crop lien of $214,600.\n\nWHY I'M WORRIED\n- Stuart, I believe you did the mother's estate plan around 2019 when she was still Mrs. Wetherington. If Lorraine is a former client and the trust is adverse, that is an RPC 1.9 problem at least.\n- Hye-jin, didn't your group represent Cascade Ridge in a labor matter last year? If they are a current client it is RPC 1.7 and we need waivers or we pass.\n- Chase says Jordan has been in treatment for an eating disorder and \"isn't in a state to run anything.\" I told him we would not be using that. Flagging so nobody is surprised if it shows up in his emails.\n- He also mentioned a possible Chapter 12 for WFO. Different engagement; do not open it yet.\n\nHe wired a $7,500 advance deposit this morning without being asked (trust account ending ...2204). I have not accepted the engagement. If we can't clear this by Thursday I'm sending it back.\n\nHis Schedule K-1 forms and the loan file are at https://files.mal-law.example/intake/wetherington-26-1183 (proposed matter no. 26-1183).\n\nThanks,\nGraciela\n\nGraciela Montenegro | Partner\nMontenegro Abimbola Lowe LLP\n32 North 3rd Street, Suite 400, Yakima, WA 98901\nd 509.555.0102 | f 509.555.0103\n\nThis message may contain privileged information. If you received it in error, delete it and tell the sender.", "kind": "Email", "detail": "432 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Graciela Montenegro", "Abimbola", "Stuart", "Hye-jin Bae", "Chase Wetherington", "Jordan Wetherington", "Lorraine Zhou", "Graciela"], "companies": ["mal-law", "Mal-law", "Abimbola Lowe LLP"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Yakima", "Wenatchee", "Tieton Drive", "Ellensburg", "WA"], "health": ["eating disorder", "Chapter 12"], "sensitive": ["family overlap", "disability", "treatment"], "names": ["Chase", "Jordan", "Stuart", "Hye-jin", "Lorraine", "Graciela", "Abimbola", "Lowe"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 2.300000000745058, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 25, "text": "Graciela Montenegro", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Graci